// `ntime`'s storage primitives — THE LAYER NOTE. This was `src/core/`'s
// placeholder (0.0.1 P-7) and the directory has been filled since cycle 0.0.4;
// the file stays because the other five placeholders point AT it for the
// explanation below, and because a layer note that a reader meets before the
// code is worth one file.
//
// WHY A PLACEHOLDER EXISTS AT ALL — the paragraph the siblings cite. An empty
// directory is invisible to the harness's `parse` sweep
// (`meta/specs/BUILD.md` §3), and the sweep is what stops the grammar being
// quietly made partial; a placeholder gives the sweep something to open. It is
// REPLACED by the cycle named in its own header, never deleted — and since
// cycle 0.0.6 `check_layering` asserts the other half mechanically: every layer
// B-17 names holds at least one `.npk`, so a directory whose placeholder was
// deleted rather than replaced is a named failure and not a smaller
// denominator (D1).
//
// WHAT FILLED THIS ONE, at cycle 0.0.4: `vec.npk` (`Vec<T>`, nine functions),
// `bytes.npk` (`Bytes`, eleven) and `limits.npk` (thirteen named bounds), per
// `BUILD.md` §5's rules B-12 and B-13 — one growable sequence, one byte sink,
// one file of named bounds, and NO second container. **This header said "It is
// REPLACED at the cycle below" and "WHEN: cycle 0.0.4" for two subcycles after
// 0.0.4 was done** (F3), which reads as work outstanding.
//
// WHAT IT MAY IMPORT: NOTHING (`BUILD.md` B-17). `core` is the base of the
// layering and every other module points at it. An import here is a layering
// violation by construction, and `check_layering` will say so from 0.0.3.
//
// THE OBLIGATION THAT ARRIVED WITH THE CODE, and how it was discharged:
// `Vec<T>.items` and `Bytes`' body are BARE POINTERS, which this language does
// not bounds-check (TM-108, `SAFETY.md` S-17b). Every accessor lays a
// length-carrying `#wild_slice` over the block and indexes THAT, so the guard
// is the compiler's own `emit_bounds_guard` and one unsigned compare rejects
// both ends (TM-129, S-17c). `check_raw_index` reports zero raw indexes in the
// library.
//
// AND THE OBLIGATION NO GATE HERE CAN DISCHARGE (S-18e, TM-139): a view from
// `bytes_view` is invalidated by growth, and a use-after-free is found by a
// WRONG ANSWER rather than by a leak gate. Read `bytes.npk`'s `bytes_view`
// before holding one.
mod:core;
